    {
      "id": "p0151-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "At first glance, this Japanese response seems to be devoid of any jokes at all. However, the English phrase \"secret shoes\" is used in Japanese to refer to what are known elsewhere as \"elevator shoes\" - shoes designed to make the wearer look taller, in other words.",
        "raw": "At first glance, this Japanese response seems to be devoid of any jokes at all.\nHowever, the English phrase \"secret shoes\" is used in Japanese to refer to what\nare known elsewhere as \"elevator shoes\" - shoes designed to make the wearer\nlook taller, in other words.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09167734,
          0.53492143,
          0.70633917,
          0.60348571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08963051,
          0.53420714,
          0.708386,
          0.60455714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          22,
          23,
          24,
          25
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "乍看之下，这段日文似乎根本没有笑点。但英语词组“secret shoes”（秘密鞋）在日语中指的正是“内增高鞋”——也就是让穿鞋的人看起来更高的鞋。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
