    {
      "id": "p0151-b010",
      "kind": "aside",
      "source": {
        "text": "I really like this Japanese shoe joke - it fits the context, it's shoe-themed, it uses the word \"secret\", and it doesn't feel forced. It all comes down to personal opinion, but I feel this is a good example of a localization surpassing the original. It does lose the discussion about souls, though.",
        "raw": "I really like this Japanese shoe joke - it fits the context, it's shoe-themed,\nit uses the word \"secret\", and it doesn't feel forced. It all comes down\nto personal opinion, but I feel this is a good example of a localization\nsurpassing the original. It does lose the discussion about souls, though.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.11192044,
          0.81498571,
          0.66652841,
          0.87272857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.11059001,
          0.81427143,
          0.66785885,
          0.8738
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          36,
          37,
          38,
          39
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "我很喜欢这个日语鞋子笑话：它符合上下文，以鞋为主题，用到了“秘密”这个词，又不显得牵强。好坏当然见仁见智，但我认为，这是一个本地化超越原文的好例子。不过，关于灵魂的那段话确实没有了。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
